Project Documentation Phase 
The Project Documentation Phase is the stage where all important information about the project is recorded in a clear and organized way.
Main steps:
Record project details – Document the project title, objectives, and purpose.
Describe the process – Explain how the project was planned and developed.
Document tools and technologies – List the software, hardware, and technologies used.
Record results – Include the outcomes and findings of the project.
Add screenshots and diagrams – Provide visual evidence of the project.
Prepare the final report – Organize all information into a complete project document.
